WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.500
Markov decision process.

2
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:07.171
Reinforcement learning chooses good actions in a world that answers back.

3
00:00:07.171 --> 00:00:09.267
This is how we describe that world.

4
00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:12.500
Here is the loop at the heart of RL.

5
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.400
The agent observes a state.

6
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.800
It picks an action.

7
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:20.533
The environment moves to a next state, drawn from transition probabilities.

8
00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:22.466
And it hands back a reward.

9
00:00:22.466 --> 00:00:23.433
Then it repeats.

10
00:00:24.633 --> 00:00:26.567
Five ingredients define the game.

11
00:00:26.867 --> 00:00:29.500
States: every situation the agent can be in.

12
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.867
Actions: the choices on the menu.

13
00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:34.600
Transitions: where an action might land you.

14
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:37.200
Reward: the only definition of good.

15
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.733
And gamma, the discount, says how much the future counts.

16
00:00:41.933 --> 00:00:43.467
Here's what the discount does.

17
00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:47.450
A reward n steps away is worth gamma to the power n today.

18
00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:49.800
The further away, the less it counts.

19
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:53.879
Typical gamma is zero point nine to zero point nine nine.

20
00:00:53.879 --> 00:00:56.067
It keeps infinite futures finite.

21
00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:58.333
Here's the payoff.

22
00:00:58.633 --> 00:01:03.794
If you can write your problem as an MDP, every algorithm in this volume applies.

23
00:01:03.794 --> 00:01:05.600
Framing it is the hard part.

24
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.700
Here is a four by four gridworld, no library.

25
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.367
A goal cell, a crater cell, and four moves.

26
00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:17.167
The step function is the transition: state and action in, next state out.

27
00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:22.200
It also returns the reward: plus one, minus one, or a tiny step cost.

28
00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.333
Picture a rover on a Mars grid.

29
00:01:25.633 --> 00:01:28.200
Cells are states and drive commands are actions.

30
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:32.867
Craters cost one point, the lander pays one, and each step burns battery.

31
00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:35.167
Q-learning then solves it unchanged.

32
00:01:36.367 --> 00:01:37.238
Let's recap.

33
00:01:37.238 --> 00:01:41.667
An MDP is states, actions, transitions, reward, and discount.

34
00:01:41.967 --> 00:01:45.267
The agent acts, the world answers with state and reward.

35
00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:47.867
Gamma decides how much the future counts.

36
00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:51.755
Frame it as an MDP and every algorithm applies.

37
00:01:51.755 --> 00:01:52.900
Next up: state.
